From: Kitsune <km2077@foxmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: support VLAN rewrite on bridge offload

Stage 1 only offloads bridge flows whose egress port emits the FDB VID
untagged. A VLAN-filtering bridge such as pon0:t (VLAN 3114 tagged) plus
lan1:u* (untagged) therefore keeps the upstream direction in the software
bridge even though the PPE can forward it.

Teach the promote path to push an 802.1Q tag on the bridged egress. The
egress action is resolved from the bridge when the FDB entry is added:
br_vlan_get_info_rcu() gives the port membership and the untagged flag,
br_vlan_get_pvid_rcu() gives the PVID. The template uses the same
data.vlan/IB1 VLAN_LAYER fields as the netfilter FLOW_ACTION_VLAN_PUSH
path, so the PPE writes vlan1 = VID and the frame leaves tagged.

This is opt-in through the vlan_rewrite module parameter, default 0: an
image can carry the code while stage-1 forwarding stays unchanged. When it
is 1, untagged-in/tagged-out flows are offloaded and counted in
fdb_stats.vlan_push. Same-VID tagged-in/tagged-out flows either keep the
tag already in the packet (LAN egress only) or push it back when it only
exists in the skb metadata; keeping the packet tag is excluded on PON
egress because the GEM lookup needs a data->vlan entry, which would ask
the PPE to push a second tag.

Tag pop is not implemented. There is no strip/remove bit or TPID field in
struct airoha_foe_l2b or the AIROHA_FOE_IB1/IB2 definitions, and the
existing code treats FLOW_ACTION_VLAN_POP as a no-op. Tagged-in/
untagged-out therefore still increments fdb_stats.vlan_pop and stays in
software. The exact hardware question is documented next to the decision:
does an L2B egress template with VLAN_LAYER=0 and empty vlan1/vlan2 strip
the ingress tag, or does it leave it in the frame? No bit is invented
here; that direction must be measured on a board first.

The PON GEM/T-CONT resolution in patch 925 already uses the last entry of
data->vlan, i.e. the egress VID. Filling data->vlan for a pushed tag is
what makes a 3114 push resolve to the GEM configured for 3114; without it
the lookup falls back to AIROHA_PON_VID_ANY. No change to 925 is needed,
but the flow is only accepted when all eight P-bits resolve to one GEM, as
before.

The switchdev bridge helpers are compiled only when CONFIG_BRIDGE and
CONFIG_BRIDGE_VLAN_FILTERING are reachable. A NET_AIROHA=y + BRIDGE=m +
NET_DSA=n build would otherwise leave an unresolved br_vlan_get_*_rcu()
symbol in vmlinux; with the guard it compiles and the push path simply
stays disabled.

The pushed tag is 802.1Q with PCP 0. br_vlan_get_info_rcu() does not
expose a per-VLAN PCP and the netfilter path does not encode act->vlan.prio
either (AIROHA_FOE_IB2_PCP is a single bit and is never set), so a non-zero
PCP cannot be reproduced yet; measure it before enabling the parameter on
a network that uses PCP.

Signed-off-by: Kitsune <km2077@foxmail.com>
---

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.h b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.h
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.h
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.h
@@ -606,6 +606,23 @@
 
 	struct airoha_fdb_key key;
 	struct net_device *egress;
+
+	/* Egress VLAN action, resolved when the FDB entry is added (and
+	 * refreshed on every promotion, because a bridge VLAN flag change does
+	 * not re-add the FDB entry). @vlan_proto is the bridge protocol in host
+	 * order; 0 means "not known / no VLAN filtering". @pcp is the PCP the
+	 * driver can reproduce, which is only 0 today: the bridge API exposes
+	 * no per-VLAN PCP and the PCP of a pushed tag comes from the per-packet
+	 * skb priority. See airoha_ppe_fdb_set_egress_vlan(). @egress_pvid is
+	 * recorded for diagnostics and future PVID-based decisions; the tag
+	 * action itself only needs @egress_untagged and @vlan_proto.
+	 */
+	u16 vlan_proto;
+	u8 egress_member:1;
+	u8 egress_untagged:1;
+	u8 egress_pvid:1;
+	u8 egress_pon:1;
+	u8 pcp:3;
 };
 
 struct airoha_wdma_info {
@@ -767,7 +784,10 @@
 	struct {
 		unsigned long promoted;     /* L2 flows promoted from the FDB */
 		unsigned long no_entry;     /* no FDB entry for the destination */
-		unsigned long vlan_rewrite; /* tag push/pop needed, see promote */
+		unsigned long vlan_rewrite; /* rewrite needed, left to software */
+		unsigned long vlan_push;    /* tag pushed by the PPE */
+		unsigned long vlan_pop;     /* pop needed, still software */
+		unsigned long vlan_skip;    /* unsupported rewrite, software */
 		unsigned long no_npu;       /* NPU not configured, promote skipped */
 	} fdb_stats;
 
diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c
@@ -57,6 +57,35 @@
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(fdb_refresh_period,
 		 "Inspect the offloaded bridge FDB entries every N seconds (0 = off)");
 
+/* Opt-in VLAN tag push on the bridged egress.
+ *
+ * 0 (the default) keeps the stage-1 behaviour: only destinations whose
+ * egress bridge port emits the FDB VID untagged are offloaded. 1 additionally
+ * lets the PPE push an 802.1Q tag when an untagged frame arrives on an access
+ * port and leaves through a tagged port (e.g. lan1:u* -> pon0:t with VLAN
+ * 3114). Tag pop is not implemented (see the TODO in
+ * airoha_ppe_bridge_fdb_promote() and DEFECT-FIXES.md), so a tagged ingress
+ * frame with an untagged egress still stays in the software bridge even when
+ * this is enabled.
+ *
+ * The parameter exists because the L2B tag handling has not been validated on
+ * hardware. Keeping it 0 in an image ships the code without changing the
+ * forwarding of a bridge that worked with stage 1.
+ */
+static bool vlan_rewrite;
+module_param(vlan_rewrite, bool, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(vlan_rewrite,
+		 "Allow the PPE to push 802.1Q tags on bridge egress (0 = off)");
+
+/* FDB statistics are approximate and can be lost on races, like the rest of
+ * the counters in this file; WRITE_ONCE() only keeps the compiler from
+ * merging or reordering them.
+ */
+static void airoha_ppe_fdb_stat_inc(unsigned long *counter)
+{
+	WRITE_ONCE(*counter, *counter + 1);
+}
+
 static int airoha_ppe_get_num_stats_entries(struct airoha_ppe *ppe)
 {
 	if (!IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_NET_AIROHA_FLOW_STATS))
@@ -1213,35 +1242,77 @@
 	return 0;
 }
 
